{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"crabby-heroic-pigeon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`models_at_or_above` and `largest_window_tokens` locate the starting rung by substring-matching\n`MODEL_LADDER`'s Anthropic family names against the primary model\n(src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:373-374). A primary from any OTHER family matches nothing,\nfalls through to sizing.py:376, and the function returns the WHOLE ladder starting at the\ntrivial rung.\n\nREPRODUCED on the tree (no class table configured):\n\n    models_at_or_above('bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0')\n      -> ['claude-haiku-4-5', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', 'claude-opus-4-8']\n    largest_window_tokens('bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0')\n      -> 1000000\n\nTwo distinct harms:\n\n1. **Escalation DOWNGRADES.** A context-limit escalation is supposed to move to a LARGER window.\n   For a non-Anthropic primary the first \"escalation\" rung is `claude-haiku-4-5` — a smaller\n   window AND a different provider family than the model the operator configured.\n2. **The window is overstated.** `largest_window_tokens` returns the ladder maximum (1000000)\n   for a model that is not in the ladder at all, so the P8 size gate under-blocks: material that\n   will not fit is judged to fit.\n\nContrast with a correctly-located primary, same tree:\n\n    models_at_or_above('anthropic:claude-opus-4-8')            -> ['claude-opus-4-8']\n    models_at_or_above('bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8-v1:0') -> ['claude-opus-4-8']\n\n## Relationship to 7de4 — different mechanism, deliberately separate\n\n7de4 is about a rung's TARGET (`_rung_target` resolving to a bare Anthropic id because the run's\nactual model is never an input). This ticket is about rung LOCATION (which rung the ladder walk\nstarts from). 7de4's plan explicitly scopes this out and pins the location behaviour byte-for-byte\nunchanged, so the two can land independently in either order.\n\n## Approach\n\nDecide the start rung by a means that does not assume the Anthropic family. Options to weigh in\nthe plan: consult the model's real context window via the profile/capability seam rather than a\nname substring; or make the miss EXPLICIT (no match -> do not escalate, and let the existing\n`_too_big` finding at sizing.py:450-471 surface) instead of silently returning the full ladder.\nA silent full-ladder fallback is the specific behaviour to eliminate — it is indistinguishable\nfrom a correct answer at the call site.\n\n`largest_window_tokens` must stop reporting the ladder maximum for a model it cannot locate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: For a primary the ladder cannot locate, escalation never proposes a rung whose context\n  window is smaller than the primary's.\n- AC2: `largest_window_tokens` does not return the ladder maximum for a model absent from the\n  ladder; an unlocatable model yields a defensible value or an explicit failure, not the max.\n- AC3: A non-Anthropic-family primary (e.g. `bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0`) does not produce\n  an escalation list beginning at a smaller-window Anthropic rung. A regression test pins this\n  with that exact id.\n- AC4: Behaviour for an Anthropic-family primary, qualified or bare, is unchanged — pinned by\n  test for both `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` and `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8-v1:0`.\n- AC5: make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default test selection is green.","id":"48b3-37ba-51a3-42db","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Context-limit escalation mis-locates the START rung for a non-Anthropic-family primary: it downgrades the window and jumps provider family"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785643194619354001,"uuid":"b829b045-a41a-4182-9b42-5c2da7db2339"}